  "description": "No. 11 Charles Street West is a charming 1920s mid terrace residence, superbly positioned adjacent to the much sought after Ormond Square development in the heart of Dublin city centre, just minutes from the Four Courts. Steeped in history, Charles Street West forms part of a collection of homes built by Dublin Corporation between c. 1920s by Architect Charles J. McCarthy.\n\nThe property offers well-proportioned accommodation throughout, comprising a spacious living room to the front, a well fitted shower room off the hallway and an extended eat in kitchen to the rear. There is a small patio yard to the rear.\n\nUpstairs, there are two generous double bedrooms, with one overlooking the front and the other positioned to the rear.\nIdeally suited to those seeking a characterful city centre home in a mature residential setting, No. 11 Charles Street West offers excellent access to a wealth of amenities, transport links and recreational facilities.\n\nAccommodation\n\nSpacious front living room\nExtended kitchen to the rear\nWell fitted shower room\nTwo generous double bedrooms\n\n\nDirections : \nCharles Street West & Ormond Square enjoys a superb city centre setting, with easy access to the Four Courts, River Liffey, and a wide range of cafes, restaurants, shops and cultural amenities. Smithfield, Stoneybatter and Capel Street are all within walking distance, while the nearby Red Line LUAS offers excellent connectivity. The redeveloped Fruit and Vegetable Market is also moments away, due to reopen in 2027 with approximately 80 food stalls, restaurants, cafes, event spaces and an outdoor farmers market.\nDIRECTIONS:\nD07 VY05",
